Title: The Last Cue
Credit: Original fictional TestFlight demo
Author: Production Desk demo content
Notes: Maya and Leo are adult college students. No real people or proprietary script are depicted.

INT. COLLEGE BLACK-BOX THEATRE - DAY #1#

MAYA, an adult student stage manager, places a prop notebook on a desk. A chair faces a practical lamp. LEO, an adult student lighting operator, checks the lamp's cable.

MAYA
Desk, chair, notebook, lamp. Nothing here has to improvise.

LEO
Good. The lamp has stronger opinions than I do.

MAYA
Stand by lighting cue twelve. We take it from the page turn.

INT. COLLEGE LIGHTING BOOTH - DAY #2#

Leo watches Maya turn a page onstage. The practical lamp stays dark. He checks the cue list beside his lighting console.

LEO
I missed twelve. I was watching for your hand, not the page.

MAYA
Then we found it in rehearsal. Hold there.

LEO
Page turn, then the lamp. I've marked it.

INT. COLLEGE BLACK-BOX THEATRE - DAY #3#

Maya resets the chair and closes the prop notebook. Leo returns to his position. She opens the notebook, turns the page, and the practical lamp glows on cue.

MAYA
Reset complete. Stand by twelve... go.

LEO
Twelve is in.

MAYA
And that's the last cue. Same again after the break.

They leave the desk ready for the next rehearsal.
